<body>
    <h1>Meeting Minutes of 2026/6/8</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p local-id=3D"84eb9470e97f">Hi all,</p>
<p local-id=3D"28a44faf7fdb">Thank you so much for your attendance. Please =
kindly check the meeting minutes below.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e20e70a85f92">Date: Monday, 8th June, 2026</p>
<p local-id=3D"df5a8b140f1c">Time: 17:30</p>
<p local-id=3D"7b82e5bbf6c1">Attendees: Tao Huang, Loura Guo, Jiajin Zhong,=
 Daijiang Xie, Yixi Wang, Suijie Song, Guangyuan Mu, Huifang Liu, Jiaxing D=
ai</p>
<p local-id=3D"1422b8dafe39">Quick Recap</p>
<p local-id=3D"bb8ac7200389">This meeting mainly focused on the module divi=
sion and development plan for the =E6=B1=87=E4=B8=B0=E7=A7=91=E6=8A=80=E8=
=8F=81=E8=8B=B1=E8=AE=AD=E7=BB=83=E8=90=A5 =E2=80=93 AI=E6=99=BA=E8=83=BD=
=E9=97=AE=E7=AD=94=E5=8A=A9=E6=89=8B project.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e01ea04af2bb">Yixi led the discussion on module division bas=
ed on the current system architecture. The team tentatively divided the sys=
tem into five major modules: data persistence layer, data processing pipeli=
ne, tool set layer, web layer, and agent integration layer. Each module own=
er introduced their technical background, preferred direction, and possible=
 contribution to the project.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a3ddeea945e8">The team also discussed whether the modules sh=
ould be developed in parallel or strictly according to dependency order. Af=
ter discussion, the team tentatively agreed to start with parallel developm=
ent for efficiency, while adjusting the collaboration model if dependency i=
ssues arise later.</p>
<p local-id=3D"03772056dd99">Vincent emphasized that the team should focus =
on the time constraints and deliverables of the first phase in July, avoid =
over-designing the system at the early stage, and clarify the specific obje=
ctives of each module for Phase 1. He also suggested that team members make=
 good use of AI tools to improve development and documentation efficiency.<=
/p>
<p local-id=3D"099c14fb2487">The meeting concluded that each module owner s=
hould define the expected Phase 1 functions, deliverables, and acceptance c=
riteria before Wednesday, and prepare a four-phase development plan for the=
 next meeting.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9188aa1cc13c">Discussion Summary</p>
<p local-id=3D"e254d0b8c841">Vincent and Tao discussed the project timeline=
 arrangement. The original plan was to arrange a session around 11th June, =
but the exact time still depends on ERC=E2=80=99s availability. Vincent men=
tioned that he would confirm the schedule with ERC and notify the team in a=
dvance. He also reminded the team to focus on the July Phase 1 deadline and=
 avoid spending too much time on overly complex designs at this stage.</p>
<p local-id=3D"181a6616dc98">Yixi introduced the proposed module division p=
lan. Based on the current architecture, the project will be divided into fi=
ve modules: data persistence layer, data processing pipeline, tool set laye=
r, web layer, and agent integration layer. The team agreed that module-base=
d division can improve development efficiency, while members with extra cap=
acity may support other modules later.</p>
<p local-id=3D"8100fc0d9cfe">The team discussed the development sequence of=
 different modules. One option is to develop the modules strictly according=
 to dependencies, starting from data persistence and data processing. Anoth=
er option is to let different modules proceed in parallel and resolve depen=
dency issues through interface definitions, mock data, and later integratio=
n. The team tentatively agreed to proceed with parallel development first.<=
/p>
<p local-id=3D"9dde67afadd3">Daijiang shared knowledge related to MCP, whic=
h stands for Model Context Protocol. He introduced the basic interaction me=
chanism between AI agents and external tools, including how the LLM communi=
cates with the MCP client, how requests are passed to the MCP server, and h=
ow backend tools are invoked. Vincent suggested that the team could refer t=
o the Open Manus project to better understand the implementation of an MCP =
server. Daijiang will share related blog links with the team.</p>
<p local-id=3D"fd2c146a36d1">Vincent and Tao also provided suggestions on f=
uture AI knowledge sharing. They suggested that when introducing technical =
concepts, especially abbreviations such as MCP, the presenter should first =
explain the full name and provide enough background information so that all=
 team members can follow the discussion more easily.</p>
<p local-id=3D"56d9435df7de">The team members introduced their technical ba=
ckgrounds and module preferences. Daijiang introduced his experience in RAG=
, embedding applications, data processing, data governance, database design=
, and AI-assisted engineering tools. Jiajin introduced his experience in Py=
thon, databases, and data processing pipelines. Jiaxing introduced his expe=
rience related to tool set development and keyword-based retrieval. Other m=
embers also discussed their possible roles in the project.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b4d0d1a45faf">The final module responsibility arrangement wa=
s discussed as follows. Suijie will be responsible for the web layer. Jiaxi=
ng will be responsible for the tool set layer. Yixi will prioritize the dat=
a persistence layer to provide basic interfaces for the data processing pip=
eline. Daijiang will be responsible for the agent integration layer. Jiajin=
 will be responsible for the data processing pipeline.</p>
<p local-id=3D"872880b9aed5">The team also discussed the four-phase develop=
ment plan. For the first phase, the focus should be on clarifying the minim=
um deliverables and building the basic framework of each module. Later phas=
es may include deeper integration, optimization, and more advanced features=
. Vincent suggested that the team should consider adding some highlight fea=
tures in later demonstrations, such as improving data search accuracy throu=
gh wiki-style organization or similar mechanisms.</p>
<p local-id=3D"be158a375e8f">Action Items</p>
<p local-id=3D"5f9ed0baa774">All team members:</p>
<p local-id=3D"dca16837ba65">Continue implementation based on the module-ba=
sed division of work.</p>
<p local-id=3D"db483832bb9d">All team members:</p>
<p local-id=3D"f00d5d284921">Make sure each function point has a clear owne=
r, and each module has clear internal responsibility division.</p>
<p local-id=3D"734c9506c486">All module owners:</p>
<p local-id=3D"3a3a4a76b640">Communicate with module partners and further c=
larify detailed module-level task division.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ae99bca4e883">All module owners:</p>
<p local-id=3D"3f224e209f11">Define the objectives, deliverables, and accep=
tance criteria for each phase, especially Phase 1 in July.</p>
<p local-id=3D"95191673e9a4">All module owners:</p>
<p local-id=3D"bdd4b1b2f15d">Prepare a four-phase development plan and pres=
ent it in the next weekly meeting.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2c972050fc02">All module owners:</p>
<p local-id=3D"278255727784">Submit or clarify the expected Phase 1 functio=
ns before Wednesday.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ae7fa3182d5e">Vincent:</p>
<p local-id=3D"283fa733c644">Confirm ERC=E2=80=99s available time and notif=
y the team in advance.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2397dbc3bedc">Vincent:</p>
<p local-id=3D"1ed4487493e9">Share the Open Manus project link in the comme=
nt section for team members to study the implementation of MCP server.</p>
<p local-id=3D"547bbe6f1532">Suijie:</p>
<p local-id=3D"9b877626d6c6">Take responsibility for the development of the=
 web layer.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c69753ee349f">Jiaxing:</p>
<p local-id=3D"580aad8157ac">Take responsibility for the development of the=
 tool set layer.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2bcfbd0f3456">Yixi:</p>
<p local-id=3D"ae744b3271e8">Prioritize the development of the data persist=
ence layer and provide basic interface support for the data processing pipe=
line.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c39df1592387">Daijiang:</p>
<p local-id=3D"9a1f6aa15736">Share MCP-related blog links in the comment se=
ction for team members=E2=80=99 reference.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2fcbb047a24a">Daijiang:</p>
<p local-id=3D"69343ced750f">Take responsibility for the development of the=
 agent integration layer.</p>
<p local-id=3D"089b1cced071">Daijiang:</p>
<p local-id=3D"98e36a463b72">When sharing AI knowledge in the future, expla=
in the full name of abbreviations when they are first mentioned, such as MC=
P, so that all team members can better understand the topic.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4c668d2054b4">Jiajin:</p>
<p local-id=3D"76a9641a8c3e">Take responsibility for the development of the=
 data processing pipeline.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b141312ac50b">Reference Links / Materials</p>
<p local-id=3D"b5cebe814a4d">Open Manus project link: To be shared by Vince=
nt.</p>
<p local-id=3D"8d9a702ea2ea">MCP-related blog links: To be shared by Daijia=
ng.</p>
<p local-id=3D"8d97a14cabad">Module division / architecture diagram: To be =
shared later if available.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b469574d42ec">Four-phase development plan: To be updated by =
each module owner and presented in the next weekly meeting.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
